Z||000000||Sage||12-02-1999||10:45 AM||||Just wanted to take a minute to thank everyone that responded to my request for suggestions about getting a title for our 86GT. Thanks go to Phil,Chadman,DJRice and Kel. If I forgot to mention anybody that responded, my apologies.  Got the title today and it is free and clear!  Now I just have to come up with funds to transfer it and buy more tags and insurance! Again thanks for all the suggestions.  Good to know that there are still people willing to help each other out.  To think that a little plasic car could bring people together, that otherwise might have had nothing to do with each other...I think that's GREAT!  A special thanks to Cliff for giving us all a place for it to happen!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||GWMORGAN||12-02-1999||12:32 PM||||Nice work Sage...how did you go about aquiring the title?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||12-02-1999||03:09 PM||||Didn't do anyhting out of the ordinary. Just kept bugging the guy to get it done.  I told him he could apply for a lost title and he said he didn't know he could do this!  Also called the magistrate and they paid him a visit, I think that kinda "pushed" him a little.  Anyway, it turned out like it should have 7 mos. ago!  That's what procrastination does.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 12-02-1999).]||||reg||1
